The `interview` lane requests on `small` and then forks on `big`.

A lane is a role on a substrate, fixed for the run, and the rule does not care
which kind of row moved it. `lane-changes-substrate.jsonl` covers two requests;
this covers a request and a fork, because the check reads both row kinds into
one map and dropping the fork arm would leave the other fixture passing.

A different lane and the other direction, deliberately: the harness refuses a
fixture whose refusal message another fixture already produces, and the first
version of this one named the same lane and the same two substrates.
